---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../../../components/ContactCTA.astro';

export const prerender = false;
---

<Layout title="A conversion problem that was a measurement problem — Juanse Barrio" description="Case study: redesign of Banco Galicia's package upgrade flow. From an embedded webview to a native experience that first decides who gets to see what." noindex>

  <script is:inline>
    if (sessionStorage.getItem('portfolio-auth') !== 'true') {
      document.documentElement.style.visibility = 'hidden';
      window.location.replace('/en/portfolio?unlock=1');
    }
  </script>

  <div class="page-container">

    <!-- ── HERO ── -->
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">CASE STUDY · BANCO GALICIA · 2026</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">A conversion problem that was a measurement problem</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Redesign of the bank's package upgrade flow: from an embedded webview to a native experience that first decides who gets to see what.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── 30-SECOND SUMMARY ── -->
    <div class="resumen">
      <div class="resumen-col">
        <p class="resumen-eyebrow">THE PROBLEM</p>
        <p class="resumen-frase">Official conversion was 6%, but 70% of the people entering the funnel had no available offer. The number measured nothing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="resumen-col">
        <p class="resumen-eyebrow">THE DECISION</p>
        <p class="resumen-frase">Offer evaluation as an entry prerequisite and a native 3-step flow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="resumen-col">
        <p class="resumen-eyebrow">THE OUTCOME</p>
        <p class="resumen-frase">Flow designed, validated and built. It didn't reach production before I left the bank.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── THE DIAGNOSIS ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE DIAGNOSIS</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-titulo">The 6% hid an 80%</h2>
      <p class="body-text">The upgrade flow lived in a SPA embedded as a webview inside the app. The experience was inconsistent with the native design system and official conversion was 6%.</p>
      <p class="body-text">That number explained nothing. I processed the customer databases with AI to reconstruct the real funnel and found that 70% of the users entering it had no available offer: they were browsing without being able to buy. Among those who did have an offer, conversion was 20%. Real dropout among eligible users was 80%.</p>
      <p class="body-text">That data changed the project's question. It wasn't how to push 6% higher. It was how to measure real intent and design only for those who could convert.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── DESIGN DECISIONS ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE DECISIONS</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-titulo">Four decisions, with their cost</h2>
      <p class="intro-text">I led the design team end to end: problem mapping, scope, flows and high-fidelity prototypes. I worked with Melanie on content design and with Nico, from the design system team, on custom components validated to scale across the bank. I used AI to analyze benchmarks and explore screen variants before defining the final flow. Technical constraints and business rules came out of the work with product and engineering.</p>

      <div class="decisiones">

        <div class="decision">
          <span class="decision-num">01</span>
          <div class="decision-body">
            <h3 class="decision-titulo">Offer as a prerequisite</h3>
            <p class="decision-texto">The finding: 70% of traffic had no offer. The decision: evaluate the offer before letting anyone in. No offer, no funnel. The alternative was to keep showing the catalog to everyone and live with dirty metrics. The cost: the flow's traffic would drop by about 70% overnight. It was the hardest decision to defend internally, because it changed how the team measured success.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <span class="decision-num">02</span>
          <div class="decision-body">
            <h3 class="decision-titulo">No plan comparator</h3>
            <p class="decision-texto">The previous flow worked like a store: every package for everyone. The new version shows only the customer's offer. The comparator moved outside the funnel, as a separate discovery surface. You lose in-context comparison. You gain measurable intent: whoever enters, enters to convert.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <span class="decision-num">03</span>
          <div class="decision-body">
            <h3 class="decision-titulo">3-step flow</h3>
            <p class="decision-texto">Evaluation, selection, confirmation. I cut intermediate product-education steps: whoever gets here already passed the offer filter. Every extra screen was an exit point with no function.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="decision last">
          <span class="decision-num">04</span>
          <div class="decision-body">
            <h3 class="decision-titulo">100% native</h3>
            <p class="decision-texto">Rebuilding the SPA was the cheap option. Going native cost more development, but it enabled the updated design system, better performance and per-step event tracking. Without that tracking, the new funnel would be as blind as the old one.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── THE FLOW IN SCREENS ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE FLOW</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-titulo">Three steps, no detours</h2>
      <div class="pantallas-wrapper">
        <div class="pantallas">
          <figure class="pantalla">
            <img src="/images/portfolio/upgrade/02-ingreso-flujo.png" alt="Entry from home" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption>ENTRY FROM HOME</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="pantalla">
            <img src="/images/portfolio/upgrade/03-animacion-flujo.png" alt="Offer evaluation" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption>OFFER EVALUATION</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="pantalla">
            <img src="/images/portfolio/upgrade/04-carrousel-flujo.png" alt="Package selection" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption>PACKAGE SELECTION</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="pantalla">
            <img src="/images/portfolio/upgrade/05-seleccion-flujo.png" alt="Terms and benefits" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption>TERMS &amp; BENEFITS</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="pantalla">
            <img src="/images/portfolio/upgrade/06-feedback-flujo.png" alt="Success confirmation" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption>SUCCESS CONFIRMATION</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── FUNCTIONAL PROTOTYPE ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">PROTOTYPE</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-titulo">The full flow, in motion</h2>
      <p class="intro-text">High-fidelity prototype built in Figma, used to validate the flow with product, engineering and business before moving to development.</p>
      <div class="video-wrapper">
        <video
          src="/images/portfolio/upgrade/07-video-final.mp4"
          poster="/images/portfolio/upgrade/07-video-poster.webp"
          autoplay
          muted
          loop
          playsinline
        ></video>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── STATUS ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">STATUS</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-titulo">How far it got</h2>
      <p class="body-text">The design passed validation with product and engineering and the flow was fully built as a native experience. It didn't reach production before I left the bank.</p>
      <p class="body-text">What was left in place: conversion measured on real offers instead of total traffic, the native flow on the current design system, and per-step event tracking.</p>
      <p class="body-text">Designing a funnel doesn't start at the screen: it starts with the logic of who gets to see what. The decision with the most impact was the one you can't see.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── NAVIGATION ── -->
    <nav class="nav-casos">
      <a href="/en/portfolio" class="nav-link">← View all cases</a>
      <a href="/en/portfolio/csat-semantico" class="nav-link">Next case: CSAT with AI →</a>
    </nav>

    <ContactCTA lang="en" />

  </div>

</Layout>

<style>
  .page-container {
    max-width: 80rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }

  /* ── HERO ── */
  .hero {
    padding-top: 8rem;
    padding-bottom: 6rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero-title {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #f0f0f0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #a0a0a0;
    max-width: 50rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
  }

  /* ── SUMMARY ── */
  .resumen {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    background: #141414;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 3rem;
    margin-top: 6rem;
  }

  .resumen-eyebrow {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .resumen-frase {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #f0f0f0;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── SECTIONS ── */
  .seccion {
    margin-top: 8rem;
  }

  .seccion .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .seccion-titulo {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #f0f0f0;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .body-text {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #c0c0c0;
    max-width: 50rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .intro-text {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #c0c0c0;
    max-width: 50rem;
    margin: 0 0 3rem;
  }

  /* ── DECISIONS ── */
  .decisiones {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .decision {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 2.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .decision.last {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .decision-num {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .decision-titulo {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #f0f0f0;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .decision-texto {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #c0c0c0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── SCREENS ── */
  .pantallas-wrapper {
    overflow-x: auto;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .pantallas {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    min-width: 900px;
  }

  .pantalla {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .pantalla img {
    width: 100%;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 16px;
    border: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
    background: #141414;
  }

  .pantalla figcaption {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* ── VIDEO ── */
  .video-wrapper {
    width: 100%;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    background: #0a0a0a;
  }

  .video-wrapper video {
    height: max(85vh, 800px);
    width: auto;
    max-width: 100%;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 24px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ── BULLETS ── */
  .bullets {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 55rem;
  }

  .bullets li {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #c0c0c0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .bullet-dash {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  /* ── NAVIGATION ── */
  .nav-casos {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 10rem;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
    padding-top: 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
  }

  .nav-link {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .nav-link:hover {
    color: #f0f0f0;
  }

  /* ── RESPONSIVE ── */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .resumen {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
      padding: 2rem;
    }

    .pantallas-wrapper {
      padding-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .pantallas {
      scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }

    .pantalla {
      scroll-snap-align: start;
      min-width: 200px;
    }

    .decision {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .decision-num {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    .nav-casos {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
